This crate (`symphonia-codec-siren`) is a pure-Rust Siren / G.722.1 decoder. It is licensed under
the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

The bitstream parsing, the vector quantizer centroids and Huffman trees (`src/tables.rs`,
extracted programmatically), the noise substitution, the frame error concealment, the Windows Live
Messenger ("MSN Siren") variant (its header, checksum and noise filling), and the transform and
overlap-add structure follow FFmpeg's `libavcodec/siren.c`, which is distributed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later:

Copyright (c) 2012 Youness Alaoui <kakaroto@kakaroto.homelinux.net>
Copyright (c) 2018 Paul B Mahol
Copyright (c) 2019 Lynne <dev@lynne.ee>

The bit allocation ("categorize"), including its adjustment for bit rates above one bit per
sample, and the parameters of the 14 kHz mode (G.722.1 Annex C: 28 regions, 640 sample frames, 5
rate control bits) follow the ITU-T G.722.1 reference decoder from Polycom, as rendered by Steve
Underwood's `libg722_1` (https://github.com/freeswitch/libg7221, LGPL-2.1+), which was also used as
the oracle for the Siren 14 and 24/32/48 kbps test vectors:

(C) 2004 Polycom, Inc. All rights reserved.

The LGPL-2.1+ terms apply to those derived portions.
